.wiki/.wikiignore exclusion subsystem: a single repo-root-anchored matcher (fail-closed on malformed patterns and on parent-exclusion re-include) that all three index passes and the check/discovery surfaces apply identically. Two freshness signals keep it honest: the worktree fast-gate folds the .wikiignore mtime, and a persisted state-row content hash triggers bidirectional Tree reconciliation (via head_tree_markdown_entries) so an un-ignore re-adds paths to --source head/index as well as ignore removing them.
